						<!-- #BeginEditable "PageBody" --><p>
						<font size=3D"2">Achieve=20
						Planner is an effective productivity tool because it was designed fro=
m the ground up with=20
						key time management principles in mind.</font></p>
						<h2>
						<font size=3D"3" color=3D"#000000">
						<span style=3D"font-weight: 400">1. Capture, Organize &amp;=20
						Manage All Your Projects</span></font></h2>
						<p><font size=3D"2">In order to manage your time=20
						effectively, you need to write things down instead of using=20
						your=20
						memory to keep track of them, especially if you are=20
						dealing with multiple projects at the same time.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner is=20
						a practical system that helps you to quickly and easily capture, orga=
nize, and=20
						manage all your projects and their tasks in one central=20
						place. You'll have a to-do list that really works!</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner uses tree-like outlines,=20
						which means you can break-down large items into smaller=20
						steps using as many levels as you need.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screensho=
ts19/OutlineTabSS.png">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/OutlineTabSS-TN.png" width=3D"529" height=3D"356"></a><br>
						<font size=3D"1">Click On Image to View Larger Size</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">One of the problems with traditional=20
						to-do lists is that they tend to lump everything you=20
						need to do together into one big long list without any=20
						order or structure.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">As you get more and more things to do,=20
						your to-do list becomes bigger and more chaotic, and=20
						pretty soon you get lost in all the details. You can=92t=20
						see the forest for all the trees that are surrounding=20
						you.</font></p>
						<p><b><font size=3D"2">Separating Projects &amp; Tasks</font></b></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">That's why Achieve Planner makes a=20
						distinction between <b>projects</b> (the outcomes) and <b>tasks</b> (=
the=20
						action steps.)</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Projects are a good way to collect,=20
						group and organize tasks that are all contributing to=20
						the same common purpose. Projects are a logical =93container=94=20
						to organize related tasks.</font></p>
						<p style=3D"page-break-after:avoid"><font size=3D"2">If you=20
						follow this model for organizing your tasks, you=92ll end=20
						up with the following structure:</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">1) A <b>Master Project List</b> that=20
						contains a list of all your projects</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">2) A <b>Task List</b> for each project=20
						that contains only the tasks for that project</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/tour/MasterPr=
ojectListStructure.png" width=3D"400" height=3D"290"></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Separating projects from their tasks=20
						means that your <b>Master Project List</b> will be smaller,=20
						easier to organize and manage, and will give you an=20
						overview of all the outcomes you are working on.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Focusing on outcomes and not just actions helps y=
ou work
						 more effectively throughout the day, increasing your
						personal productivity and helping you get things done.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Your project-specific Task List helps=20
						you focus in on just the tasks for one specific project=20
						without getting distracted or overwhelmed by everything=20
						else that is on your plate.</font></p>
						<p>&nbsp;</p>
		=09
			<div align=3D"center">
				<table border=3D"1" width=3D"490" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"2" i=
d=3D"table2" class=3D"testimonial">
					<tbody><tr>
						<td>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">
						<font size=3D"2">"After trying Achieve=20
						Planner for nearly two months I can honestly=20
						say that <b>it has revolutionized the way I=20
						work</b>.</font></p>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">
						&nbsp;</p>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">
						<font size=3D"2">I have an incredibly busy=20
						schedule so I need something that can cope=20
						with a multitude of tasks, projects and=20
						appointments whilst at the same time <b>keeping=20
						me focused on what is most important</b>.=20
						Achieve Planner does all of this and much=20
						more besides. </font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Over the years I've tried=20
						pretty much every system on the market and=20
						nothing, absolutely nothing, comes anywhere=20
						close to this. It looks great, works=20
						superbly, comes with excellent instructions,=20
						is a pleasure to use, but most important of=20
						all - <b>IT REALLY WORKS!</b> </font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">For anyone who wants to=20
						get organized and take their productivity to=20
						the next level <b>Achieve Planner is an=20
						absolute must</b>. It's one piece of software=20
						that I'm certain I'll be using for many=20
						years to come."</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">- Paul Smithson</font></p></td>
					</tr>
				</tbody></table>
				</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
						<p>Video Tutorials</p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">The tour includes some video tutorials=20
						that show you how Achieve Planner works. These tutorials can take a l=
ot of screen space,=20
						so you might want to=20
enable full-screen display in Internet Explorer or Firefox by pressing the =
F11 Key. You can turn it off by pressing F11 again.</font></p>
<p><font size=3D"2">NOTE: Since Achieve Planner is updated regularly, the t=
utorials may look=20
slightly different from the version of the software you are using. The main=
=20
ideas and functionality should still be the same.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Video Tutorials (links open in new=20
						window):</font></p>
						<ul>
							<li><font size=3D"2">
							<a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/tour/GMD=
