Tasks</a> - How to define tasks for your focus projects</font></li>
						</ul>
						<p>&nbsp;</p>
						<h2><font size=3D"3" color=3D"#000000">
						<span style=3D"font-weight: 400"><a name=3D"Prioritize">2. Focus on W=
hat Is Most=20
						Important</a></span></font></h2>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner helps you prioritize your project=
s &amp;=20
						tasks using the ABCD priority system. Priorities are=20
						made up of a letter ('A', 'B', 'C' or 'D') with an=20
						optional numeric rank.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner uses=20
						customizable color-codes for each priority level, and=20
						you can use ranked ("A1") or unranked ("A") priority=20
						values.</font></p>
						<p>
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/images/Priori=
ties.png" width=3D"106" height=3D"298" align=3D"right" alt=3D"Prioritizing =
your tasks is easy using the ABCD system"><font size=3D"2">Using=20
						priorities will help you=20
						apply the 80/20 rule and spend more time on your most=20
						important/valuable projects and tasks. </font></p>
						<p>
						<font size=3D"2">You start by giving each item=20
						in your list one of four priority values:</font></p>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 5px">
						<font size=3D"2"><b>A</b> - Very important items that you=20
						need to get done</font></p>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 5px">
						<font size=3D"2"><b>B</b> - Important items that you=20
						want to do, but not as important as the A's</font></p>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 5px">
						<font size=3D"2"><b>C -</b> Items that you may want to do=20
						at some point, but not right now</font></p>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 5px">
						<font size=3D"2"><b>D -</b> Items that are not important=20
						enough to do at all</font></p>
						<p>
						</p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Next, look at all your A items and=20
						select the top five to ten most important items and give=20
						them a rank. A1 for the most important, A2 for the next=20
						most important, and so on.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">One of the advantages of=20
						separating projects and tasks is that you can prioritize=20
						them separately.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">It's much easier and=20
						effective to prioritize projects by comparing them to=20
						other projects because you are basically deciding which outcome=20
						is more important to you right now.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">It's also easier to=20
						prioritize the tasks of a project, where you are=20
						deciding what&nbsp; actions are most important for that=20
						project.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">It's much more difficult=20
						to prioritize one big, long list of tasks from different=20
						projects that are all mixed together.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">Using priorities will=20
						help you focus on what is most important.</font></p>
